      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a heavy burden to feel that a \"bad\" instinct overrode your empathy, and while that pain is real, self-judging yourself as a \"predator\" or a \"monster\" is a harsh self-stigma that often deepens the grief instead of healing it. The lack of a strong urge to help in that moment could stem from shock, a sense of helplessness that felt more profound than empathy, or simply a difficult emotional state you didn understand at the time, none of which confirm your moral core.\n\nPlease consider that these dark thoughts can sometimes be a symptom of deep depression or trauma rather than evidence of a \"broken\" soul, and you deserve support to explore those feelings with a professional who can help you understand and navigate them.",
